  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Thursday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Thunderstorms are expected to amplify this \nafternoon, although remaining weaker than those yesterday afternoon. \nThe low pressure center that\u2019s been driving our weather recently \nwill get absorbed back into the broader pattern tonight, exiting to \nthe east, but a shortwave trough following right behind it will \nspark a few final showers in Eastern Nevada Saturday. Zonal flow is \nexpected to build in behind the shortwave, allowing for dry and \nwarming conditions through the end of the forecast. Daytime \ntemperatures begin in the 50s and 60s for Saturday and are expected \nto reach the mid 80s by Wednesday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in continuing \nunsettled and wet weather today. Moderate confidence in showers on \nSaturday. Moderate confidence in zonal flow to start next week, but \nhigh confidence that zonal flow would result in dry and warming \nconditions. No adjustments made to base NBM output.",
